sync means that each statement will be executed line by line in other in which they have been written
async means a none blocking code because it does not block the execution of rest of the code.
utilities files contain reuseable function.
server file is responsible for starting the project.
database configuration: this part is responsible for the connection between the app and mongoDB.
JIO: it checks wether the submitted data follows the required rules

MODEL: defines the structure of the information stored in the database

ROUTER: define the address through which the client communicate with the backend.
CONTROLLER: it contain the main instruction for processing requests

MIDDLEWARE: it is a code that run between receiving the request and completing the response.
-checking login token
-restricting access according to the user roles
-validating incoming information
-handling error
-checking certain router parameters


HOW USER REGISTRATION WORKS

-The student submits their name, email and password
-The registration route directs the request the registration controller after validation
-The controller create the user through the user model
The password is hashed before the user record is saved
-MongoDB store the new user record
-The API return a success response and a JWT for subsequent authenticated request

COMPLAINT
this is the part of the CampusConnect where a student can lay a complain and it will be view by the support office or administration before giving response to the student through vai email or otherwise.

HOW THE ADMINISTRATION DASHBOARD WORKS 
-The administration dashboard uses data received from the database to show summary information.